TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` attributes with a hook-type enum to control scope. Here's a sketch for each:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // runs after each [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void MyTest() { }
}
```

## 2. Once Per Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void MyTest() { }
}
```

> **Note:** Class-level hooks must be `static`.

## 3. Once Per Assembly (assembly-level)

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // once before any test in the assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // once after all tests in the assembly
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it automatically.

## 4. Once Per Test Session (global)

```csharp
public class SessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very first thing in the entire test run
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very last thing in the entire test run
    }
}
```

---

### Summary table

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? | Context parameter |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No | `TestContext` (optional) |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes | `TestSessionContext` |

All hooks support `async Task` return types. The enum values come from `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` (or qualify as `HookType.Test`, etc.).
